{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/780","id":4750810194,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPo01Gc8AAAABGyucUg","html_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/780","diff_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/780.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/780.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/issues/780","number":780,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use bespoke quantities throughout radix sorting","user":{"login":"segovb","id":70238035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjM4MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70238035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb","html_url":"https://github.com/segovb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The GPU (graphics processor) sorter used primitive integers for item counts,\nkey widths and other quantities with different meanings. Its migration also\nneeds to reach unchanged producers and consumers so those contracts remain\nconsistent across complete operations.\n\nThe published change introduces sorting quantities for counts, widths, passes\nand digits. The continuation covers retained capacities, byte layouts and the\nbounding volume hierarchy (BVH), vertex normals, cloth self-collision,\nunderlayers, hair, fitting and their application consumers.\n\nSorting populations remain distinct from #779's launch quantities. The work\nconsumes the canonical invocation, workgroup, buffer-byte and element-stride\nowners. Shared GPU submission, copying, readback and error handling are\ncoordinated with #826 through explicit whole-function ownership. Compatibility\nadapters and competing implementations are outside the intended final API.\n\n## Current status\n\nThis pull request remains a draft. Its published head is\n`e14407cc494615f0b16522fb7aa7672a3589a3c3`. The audit continuation is local;\nits latest local commit is `c6659f6cfa4610f066c659411ade6636e21bd3b5`.\nNo continuation code has been pushed or submitted for hosted checks.\nCurrent main was reconfirmed as `990430b77a9f63548ffcb642074185f61ddb3322`;\n#779 remains at `71f9cab8a5f97760e2e61ca4c74876b715f8aebc`.\n\nLocal implementation now includes:\n\n- Checked sorting and dispatch layouts, scratch growth and exact input byte\n  prefixes. Recorded BVH views retain their actual buffers and layout, and a\n  replacement collider is published only after its initial submission succeeds.\n- Canonical submission, ranged copying and validation-scope consumers. Grouped\n  readback retains its producing device and concrete callback and polling\n  causes. Armor and fitting readbacks use named tickets and logical prefixes;\n  empty numeric reductions return a typed error.\n- Metal tile and engraving admission, immutable recipe association and checked\n  texture-map extents. Generated resource programs use explicit entry points,\n  canonical texture component projection and fallible storage-format spelling.\n- Sealed host and native strand shapes, source and device association, full\n  storage admission before resident-prefix selection, checked native identities\n  and work arrays, and source-bound simulation frames. Card geometry preserves\n  the distinction between generic triangle lists and generated strips. Atlas\n  recipes and actual mip metadata flow through their owning builders.\n- The coordinated renderer receiver, including actual source identity, typed\n  selection and frame populations, logical binding prefixes and fallible\n  simulation updates. Receiving review exposed and resolved duplicate error\n  conversion, unit-import and unused-binding integration findings.\n- One shared mesh strip owner used by the host card builder and the Creator's\n  card and ribbon paths. The Creator carries typed form ordinals, shares,\n  counts and distances through preview, export and existing fixtures. Empty\n  strand sources draw zero strands, logical reads exclude allocation padding,\n  and strip submission errors propagate. Atlas export reads each mip's actual\n  dimensions. Scoped Code, Rule and Comment Reviews found no remaining finding\n  after corrections; source comparisons preserve all four strip WGSL programs\n  and the existing fixture oracles.\n- Fixed scalp mip layouts remain attached to the actual buffer and creating\n  device through baking, readback and preview upload. Texel spans, shadow block\n  counts, storage records, byte addresses and launches have separate owners.\n  Foreign-device host reads reject before mapping. Exact source comparisons\n  preserve shader text, mip addresses, pass order and existing fixture oracles;\n  all three scoped reviews and the thirteen-lens scoped successor are clear.\n- Creator initialization caches and material/clothing receivers preserve their\n  actual error causes. Mail textures are all decoded before image handles or a\n  successful cache entry are published. Hair completion uses the canonical\n  fallible asynchronous completion API. Mesh strip row admission preserves its\n  integer-conversion cause. The two-dimensional Advect program relies on the\n  native sRGB sample conversion once, and its three-dimensional Clamp path\n  bounds the upper texture address. Each code family has scoped independent\n  Code, Rule and Comment Review evidence. A nested lockfile also records its\n  declared armor dependencies; final locked hosted validation remains pending.\n\nThese are local source-review results. They establish no compiled, runtime or\nwhole-PR acceptance. The complete combined source still needs a fresh\npost-repair wave across all thirteen lenses.\n\nRequired implementation remains in the physical/grid and GPU level producers,\nbody and fitting, armor and runtime consumers, and the remaining lower GPU\ncomposition. Receiving review also identified generated-program item-order,\nparameter-record and Stencil state-schema gaps, including unsigned value/index\nclassification inconsistencies. Their complete source-backed thirteen-lens\npreinventory records the final owner, admission, emission and caller contracts\nbefore implementation. Generated-program and extraction handoffs remain held\nuntil that connected family is complete. The coordinated lower GPU, baseline\nand armor-documentation successors await complete receiving composition. These\ndependencies remain open; earlier scoped reviews do not waive them.\n\nBruno transferred the remaining connected #774 claims to this coordinated\ncontinuation. The [ownership record](https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/774#issuecomment-6372371468)\nsupersedes the earlier missing-implementer limitation. #826 owns the agreed lower\nGPU, armor and metal facade/error functions, hair renderer and selection-policy\nfamily. #780 owns the connected producers, layouts, fitting and application\nerrors. Shared-function changes require an agreed owner; ownership does not\nestablish implementation clearance.\n\n## Validation\n\nNo new tests, test cases, test helpers, assertions or documentation tests are\nadded by the continuation. Existing fixture API changes follow the canonical\nmigration while retaining their cases and oracles. Project checks will use the\nhosted workflows after connected migration families are complete.\n\nThe ignored source-backed ledger records all thirteen lenses, contracts,\ndispositions, dependencies, repairs and acceptance criteria. Discovery,\nimplementation and validation remain distinct. Targeted source comparisons and\nscoped reviews do not substitute for complete post-repair audit waves.\n\nCompletion requires all thirteen lenses, final independent Code Review, Rule\nReview and Comment Review, and required hosted CI to pass on the same final\npushed revision. Those gates remain pending. Do not merge.\n\n## Implementation context\n\nMaterial decisions are separate sorting and launch quantities, canonical shared\nowners, checked layouts before recording, actual source and provider association,\nretained native causes, and explicit whole-function ownership across #774 and\n#826. Source preservation evidence is kept separate from pending hosted\nacceptance. No reviewed shared conversation snapshot is available for this\ncontinuation; this description is the authoritative scope and validation summary.\n\nPart of #726. Related dispatch API: #779. Shared receiving contracts: #826.\n","created_at":"2026-10-05T21:11:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T07:14:11Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/780/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/780/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/issues/780/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/statuses/e14407cc494615f0b16522fb7aa7672a3589a3c3","head":{"label":"adventure-simulator-group:codex/sort-quantities-726","ref":"codex/sort-quantities-726","sha":"e